0..68 Comment "//! This source defines the `⇝` notation for a flow between types."
69..109 Comment "//! The notation also accepts `A ~~> B`."
110..113 Comment "//!"
114..179 Comment "//! A flow represents a translator without an inverse round trip."
180..232 Comment "//! Directed univalence classifies it as a function."
233..236 Comment "//!"
237..289 Comment "//! `Flow.into` constructs a flow from a translator."
290..354 Comment "//! The checker expands the notation to `Flow[.A = Type](A, B)`."
355..358 Comment "//!"
359..438 Comment "//! - cites: [Gratzer-2026-directed_univalence_simplicial_homotopy_type_theory]"
